  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Teaching and Learning for Education Excellence in the Middle East (TALEEM)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(USAID Middle East Regional (MER)):  Through the Teaching and Learning for Education Excellence in the Middle East (TALEEM) contract, USAID seeks to conduct a variety of multi-country research, training and analytical support activities to advance student learning and success in the Middle East and North Africa (MENA). This activity will fulfill three key objectives: a) produce on-demand analyses for education strategic and programmatic development and policy reform for USAID Missions; b) test emerging, cost-effective solutions for achievement of student learning with potential to scale; and c) train USAID and education sector staff on new and emerging priorities. This activity will enable the ME Bureau to: utilize research and evidence to guide education investments in the region; support timely research, assessments, and generation of evidence; test innovative solutions for learning at scale; and support USAID&apos;s MENA Missions to achieve their strategic goals and ultimately, to aid host country governments to deliver on their commitments of education for all..This mechanism will program $2,265,000 towards the Basic Education earmark and $1,000,000 towards Basic Education for Girls in Conflict.</narrative>
  </description>
